    {
      "id": "pio8s9w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Time Period of the Vedic Age"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vedic Age is divided into the Early Vedic Period (1500–1000 BC) and the Later Vedic Period (1000–600 BC).",
        "The four sacred Vedas are Rigveda (oldest), Samaveda (chants), Yajurveda (rituals), and Atharvaveda (charms and spells).",
        "Political hierarchy developed from Kula (family) -> Grama (village) -> Vis (clan) -> Jana (people) -> Rashtra (country).",
        "Democratic assemblies like Sabha, Samiti, Vidatha, and Gana played significant political and social roles.",
        "The economy shifted from pastoralism in the Rigvedic era to settled agriculture in the Later Vedic era due to the discovery of iron."
      ],
      "id": "zhshm7z"
    },
